course: dictionary
lesson: 7205
title: Pharaoh
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pharaoh was a king of ancient Egypt. The sentence «Tutankhamun became pharaoh as a boy of about nine» tells you a pharaoh is a ruler, someone who held the crown. Ancient means very old, so this word belongs to long ago.
explain: «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head, carved from the rock next to the pyramids» gives you more clues: Egypt, pyramids and a king. Pharaoh is a title, like a job name, and it has a capital P when it is used as a name, as in «the court of Pharaoh».
explain: The same word can point to different stories. In history lessons, a pharaoh is a king of Egypt. In Bible stories, Pharaoh is the proud king of Egypt who kept the Israelites as slaves. Read the words around it to see which one it is, then swap in "king of Egypt" and check it still makes sense.
fact: A pharaoh was a king of ancient Egypt who ruled the land.
fact: Egyptians thought their pharaoh was a god.
fact: Pharaoh is spelled P-H-A-R-A-O-H, with the "a" before the "o".
fact: «Tutankhamun» became pharaoh as a boy of about nine and died at about nineteen.
fact: Pharaohs are linked to pyramids, mummies, tombs and hieroglyphs.
exercise: «Tutankhamun became pharaoh as a boy of about nine.» What is a pharaoh? | A soldier who guarded tombs | A kind of stone used for building pyramids | *A king of ancient Egypt | A teacher who wrote on papyrus
exercise: «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head.» Find and copy one word that tells you the statue is big. | lion | *huge | carved | statue
exercise: In the Bible stories, Pharaoh is the proud ruler who kept the Israelites as slaves. What is Pharaoh in these stories? | *A king of Egypt | A type of pyramid | A Roman general | A river that flows through Egypt
test: «Cleopatra VII, the last pharaoh, lived about 2,050 years ago.» What does "the last pharaoh" mean? | A pyramid built last | *The last king of Egypt to rule as pharaoh | A pharaoh who was born last | A statue of a lion
test: Which spelling of the word is correct? | Farrow | Pharoh | *Pharaoh | Pharao
exam: «In prison Joseph explained the dreams of Pharaoh's baker and cupbearer.» Whose servants were the baker and cupbearer? | Napoleon's | *Pharaoh's | Moses' | Joseph's
